{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "description": "Vigie24 reference category taxonomy with search keywords per category. The category list (slug, name, hierarchy) is taken verbatim from the official vigie24 taxonomy (src/Vigie24.Domain/Taxonomy.cs, class VigieTaxonomy). Keywords are provided for source discovery: at least 3 French and 3 English search keywords per category, plus platform-specific terms for RSS (Google News / feed directory queries), YouTube (channel discovery), Reddit (subreddit names, queried as r/<name>) and Bluesky (hashtags/search terms). Field names are English; data values are French where relevant (category names, French keywords).",
  "source": "src/Vigie24.Domain/Taxonomy.cs — VigieTaxonomy.Categories (used as-is)",
  "updated_at": "2026-08-29",
  "usage_notes": {
    "keywords": "Each category MUST have at least 3 entries in keywords.fr and keywords.en. These are the canonical search terms for the collection module (src/discovery.py).",
    "platforms": "platforms.rss/youtube/reddit/bluesky hold terms adapted to each platform. reddit entries are subreddit names (search as r/<name>). rss entries are French-first queries (vigie24 is French-speaking-first).",
    "hierarchy": "Top-level entries are parent categories (parent_slug: null); each carries a subcategories array. A flat view of all 41 categories = parents + all subcategories."
  },
